{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "voices": [
    "en-US-AndrewNeural"
  ],
  "rate": "-3%",
  "parts": [
    {
      "module": "09",
      "part": "04",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m09p04-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "cba464fab65d2f69eda48c02c99e829e62113fac4d01d09215064d295d01941e",
        "2": "e9212162838fe4ac6f9552e9cc40625045b60bd8ae41946b5affdefb86744fb5",
        "3": "e908dcd44019e92ed3af3ade73c42512cd250115958243ef993d1075617a6fc2"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m09p04-andrew-exp-s01-c1-4996e7665142",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Your app needs to read a long-retained file immediately. Which archive class can do that without a restore? Glacier Instant Retrieval serves the object in milliseconds. Weigh retrieval charges and the ninety-day minimum storage duration.",
          "text_sha256": "4996e7665142bf4d9ef1465da17f1a33b59fce9133a44bcbd28b61a3dcdc9aef",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "4996e7665142bf4d9ef1465da17f1a33b59fce9133a44bcbd28b61a3dcdc9aef",
          "asset_sha256": "cba464fab65d2f69eda48c02c99e829e62113fac4d01d09215064d295d01941e"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p04-andrew-exp-s01-c2-ec32a9973fe7",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "With Flexible Retrieval, the app cannot read the bytes right away. Start a restore, wait for it to finish, then read the restored copy. Pick a retrieval option that fits the recovery window.",
          "text_sha256": "ec32a9973fe7562867e2a75855be45a72b94ac4ec41b6d060f3c780b04ce6d3b",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "ec32a9973fe7562867e2a75855be45a72b94ac4ec41b6d060f3c780b04ce6d3b",
          "asset_sha256": "cba464fab65d2f69eda48c02c99e829e62113fac4d01d09215064d295d01941e"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p04-andrew-exp-s01-c3-f734a33785bf",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Deep Archive trades a longer retrieval lead time for lower storage cost on rarely accessed data. It also has a one-hundred-eighty-day minimum. If your restore test misses the deadline, a cheaper copy does not solve the problem.",
          "text_sha256": "f734a33785bf41a1320c7a35b4aac9c0b9bcdfe3e07bb35d26012e902ee5cbdc",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "f734a33785bf41a1320c7a35b4aac9c0b9bcdfe3e07bb35d26012e902ee5cbdc",
          "asset_sha256": "cba464fab65d2f69eda48c02c99e829e62113fac4d01d09215064d295d01941e"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p04-andrew-exp-s02-c1-66d1cf2ab3fd",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Suppose nobody opens this object for three months. If it qualifies, S three can move it from Frequent Access through Infrequent Access to Archive Instant Access. Despite the name, the automatic instant tier still serves the object without starting a restore.",
          "text_sha256": "66d1cf2ab3fd7b90caa86cc25b4c43b98d3996947a87b8e00d46d62b56d18a7d",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "ddf3064dcd18a9da39cc46549ce42e093a8cb8f46249ad8d949009ca58982beb",
          "asset_sha256": "e9212162838fe4ac6f9552e9cc40625045b60bd8ae41946b5affdefb86744fb5"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p04-andrew-exp-s02-c2-2cf12caac755",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Optional Archive Access behaves differently. Enable it only if the app can wait for a restore before reading. It can begin after ninety days without access, but it is not the automatic Archive Instant Access tier.",
          "text_sha256": "2cf12caac75584d5ec376bdb533d69e6f8c334333985f36ba848f88815eb9816",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "2cf12caac75584d5ec376bdb533d69e6f8c334333985f36ba848f88815eb9816",
          "asset_sha256": "e9212162838fe4ac6f9552e9cc40625045b60bd8ae41946b5affdefb86744fb5"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p04-andrew-exp-s02-c3-78a740580169",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Optional Deep Archive Access can start after at least a hundred eighty days without access. Here again, the app needs a restore before it can read the data.",
          "text_sha256": "78a7405801698b65df3a86baf033f2582297dd3c0642919643abd2cd33e970b7",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "78a7405801698b65df3a86baf033f2582297dd3c0642919643abd2cd33e970b7",
          "asset_sha256": "e9212162838fe4ac6f9552e9cc40625045b60bd8ae41946b5affdefb86744fb5"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p04-andrew-exp-s02-c4-55a950d964a7",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "What about lots of tiny objects? Objects under one hundred twenty-eight kilobytes stay in Frequent Access and are not monitored for automatic tiering. Check the size mix before estimating savings.",
          "text_sha256": "55a950d964a76674159e3213e9e55bcbf1feec10d3c512126215fc9ad2f9c0b7",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "55a950d964a76674159e3213e9e55bcbf1feec10d3c512126215fc9ad2f9c0b7",
          "asset_sha256": "e9212162838fe4ac6f9552e9cc40625045b60bd8ae41946b5affdefb86744fb5"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p04-andrew-exp-s03-c1-b6db01ce4dcc",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "An expiration rule on the current version can make a delete marker current. A normal read then stops finding the object, but that action does not erase the older versions.",
          "text_sha256": "b6db01ce4dcc136ae4e2f0e5097f682b7cb239cc07af5786e78fedb3d8902b0b",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "b6db01ce4dcc136ae4e2f0e5097f682b7cb239cc07af5786e78fedb3d8902b0b",
          "asset_sha256": "e908dcd44019e92ed3af3ade73c42512cd250115958243ef993d1075617a6fc2"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p04-andrew-exp-s03-c2-5ec7745c5f00",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Those older versions need their own lifecycle rule. Decide how long you might need them for recovery before expiring or transitioning them. Otherwise a routine cleanup can remove the version you'd want to restore.",
          "text_sha256": "5ec7745c5f000df30ac4ea1dc7fd2b0ef069184b526ae76f43af5c9cc0d2174f",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "5ec7745c5f000df30ac4ea1dc7fd2b0ef069184b526ae76f43af5c9cc0d2174f",
          "asset_sha256": "e908dcd44019e92ed3af3ade73c42512cd250115958243ef993d1075617a6fc2"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p04-andrew-exp-s03-c3-dc7851e87d0e",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "An expired delete marker can be cleaned up when it is eligible. Use a prefix when you need to scope marker cleanup. An expired-marker cleanup action does not accept a tag filter. Test an example key before enabling the rule.",
          "text_sha256": "dc7851e87d0ecadd3cf2c12bf7da13d356065224833caa501f550c0dee7317f9",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "dc7851e87d0ecadd3cf2c12bf7da13d356065224833caa501f550c0dee7317f9",
          "asset_sha256": "e908dcd44019e92ed3af3ade73c42512cd250115958243ef993d1075617a6fc2"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "09",
      "part": "05",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m09p05-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "a0e9e6fa69d8064da2aa1432f41b49fa367cccaa6fe8bebbf18262867ce4c322",
        "2": "ca4a2eee9d0f4901b16bcb15ad9fa894cf4837a7b62e399ade34fd2165afb830",
        "3": "b42b1bc561b63e3ea58dcae5c1bd7762eb822f3c18212e63f62618066ee0891f"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m09p05-andrew-exp-s01-c1-a20993cb9353",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "You need a copy of these objects. Should it stay in the same Region or survive a regional disruption? First make sure the source bucket is versioned. Then compare the two destinations.",
          "text_sha256": "a20993cb9353a1c8475ce9016b13d30b0f13631380b37c41fd4f2c1e12185956",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a20993cb9353a1c8475ce9016b13d30b0f13631380b37c41fd4f2c1e12185956",
          "asset_sha256": "a0e9e6fa69d8064da2aa1432f41b49fa367cccaa6fe8bebbf18262867ce4c322"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p05-andrew-exp-s01-c2-4a9b2288c9d7",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Choose Same-Region Replication when the copy must stay in the same Region. Both buckets here are in US East one, even though they are separate buckets.",
          "text_sha256": "4a9b2288c9d7e85981a9053f64c8a65c618736eff9e866c9d4849d1c714b0ce1",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "4a9b2288c9d7e85981a9053f64c8a65c618736eff9e866c9d4849d1c714b0ce1",
          "asset_sha256": "a0e9e6fa69d8064da2aa1432f41b49fa367cccaa6fe8bebbf18262867ce4c322"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p05-andrew-exp-s01-c3-babd495a3c1a",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "If the requirement calls for a second Region, choose Cross-Region Replication. In this example the destination is US West two.",
          "text_sha256": "babd495a3c1a54a0ad564c360e21e670b51ca084e31746083bbe95d2941a7c58",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "babd495a3c1a54a0ad564c360e21e670b51ca084e31746083bbe95d2941a7c58",
          "asset_sha256": "a0e9e6fa69d8064da2aa1432f41b49fa367cccaa6fe8bebbf18262867ce4c322"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p05-andrew-exp-s01-c4-9202e0524824",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Turn on versioning in both buckets so the rule has eligible object versions to copy.",
          "text_sha256": "9202e05248245317f41d0ae73eeca027322c85d23cb2f913f297467151826b86",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "9202e05248245317f41d0ae73eeca027322c85d23cb2f913f297467151826b86",
          "asset_sha256": "a0e9e6fa69d8064da2aa1432f41b49fa367cccaa6fe8bebbf18262867ce4c322"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p05-andrew-exp-s01-c5-568a90e34433",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "The replication rule and its I A M role determine what is copied and whether that copy can be written. Do not expect the rule to copy the bucket configuration.",
          "text_sha256": "568a90e3443310ab0ff9e92c36d9299ea0e77bb9b9c9ba1011f29b41a3c9cde1",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "6710bc4cb823adb9e64067616f564c9cc4128ec70d2fa97600108aa09b46edd2",
          "asset_sha256": "a0e9e6fa69d8064da2aa1432f41b49fa367cccaa6fe8bebbf18262867ce4c322"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p05-andrew-exp-s01-c6-13315a34a35b",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "If the source object uses S S E K M S, configure the supported encryption settings and key permissions. Write an eligible test object, then verify the encrypted version at the destination.",
          "text_sha256": "13315a34a35b2d1167939366a204e5084c3a44f35e42ffbe8fdd02da62373d4a",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "da3f9d04158feaa4decededc0f54fb2d9048bed055a5069d8c96e0db2406d5ee",
          "asset_sha256": "a0e9e6fa69d8064da2aa1432f41b49fa367cccaa6fe8bebbf18262867ce4c322"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p05-andrew-exp-s02-c1-bd2774eb9f22",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "A new eligible object follows the live replication path after you configure the rule. Monitor that path. If live timing matters, evaluate Replication Time Control instead of assuming the new object is already available in both buckets.",
          "text_sha256": "bd2774eb9f229e551721a1d521529ff12faf6085e414689321e434457a9057a8",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "bd2774eb9f229e551721a1d521529ff12faf6085e414689321e434457a9057a8",
          "asset_sha256": "ca4a2eee9d0f4901b16bcb15ad9fa894cf4837a7b62e399ade34fd2165afb830"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p05-andrew-exp-s02-c2-0ea60b6d08f4",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Now consider an object that was already there. A new rule does not backfill it. Run a Batch Replication job for eligible older objects or gaps. The live time control does not apply to that job.",
          "text_sha256": "0ea60b6d08f43240ffe5a1b85b7bca39610657a01a4ce65974fb78b6e5904e2e",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "0ea60b6d08f43240ffe5a1b85b7bca39610657a01a4ce65974fb78b6e5904e2e",
          "asset_sha256": "ca4a2eee9d0f4901b16bcb15ad9fa894cf4837a7b62e399ade34fd2165afb830"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p05-andrew-exp-s02-c3-097dd0469953",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "A delete marker and a version-specific delete are different. A supported rule can be set to replicate markers. Deleting a specific version in the source does not perform the same deletion at the destination.",
          "text_sha256": "097dd0469953a2dfc2c98bb7a7dda7f8b84a90c2601d2b715e8aff15d541fb24",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "097dd0469953a2dfc2c98bb7a7dda7f8b84a90c2601d2b715e8aff15d541fb24",
          "asset_sha256": "ca4a2eee9d0f4901b16bcb15ad9fa894cf4837a7b62e399ade34fd2165afb830"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p05-andrew-exp-s03-c1-bc3335bcdbcd",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "An invoice lands in S three and the app needs to process it. Start with the object-created event. The uploader can finish its own work without calling the downstream process directly.",
          "text_sha256": "bc3335bcdbcd82168dfac0ac8925a981ff9783e5c95d348e097105bbc3bfe567",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "ef5a65f4cf2ddf4b3e2f77a0065405947e882f1e1ec10b15ce1fc4ddbd8d13b1",
          "asset_sha256": "b42b1bc561b63e3ea58dcae5c1bd7762eb822f3c18212e63f62618066ee0891f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p05-andrew-exp-s03-c2-d7742dcc5329",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Match the invoices prefix and C S V suffix so the consumer receives the files it needs. These are key filters, not arbitrary wildcards. If the process writes output, keep those new keys outside the trigger scope.",
          "text_sha256": "d7742dcc53299402232d226a01bb403b8298e01f8a0951f475e3d3421d90625c",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "f7eb23c3090927a3c69b1411fb231266d725e4f6d06de8d0b0b31d067ef53d25",
          "asset_sha256": "b42b1bc561b63e3ea58dcae5c1bd7762eb822f3c18212e63f62618066ee0891f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p05-andrew-exp-s03-c3-b97eb66b64d2",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Grant permission to deliver to the chosen Lambda function, standard SQS queue, or standard SNS topic, then test receipt. If the same event comes twice, processing it twice should not create two invoice records.",
          "text_sha256": "b97eb66b64d2a3404e5d7fab0c766f8ab0723bf5af582b1bc25cfc10686611a1",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "b97eb66b64d2a3404e5d7fab0c766f8ab0723bf5af582b1bc25cfc10686611a1",
          "asset_sha256": "b42b1bc561b63e3ea58dcae5c1bd7762eb822f3c18212e63f62618066ee0891f"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "09",
      "part": "06",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m09p06-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "8ba94a674d400e16b6810258fa83bae4375e00b24f7cbc47c66ac2475dbe547b",
        "2": "37ca4d9c86dbd60bdf8a4ce35067098edf819dc0743a526f5298df31ede5878c",
        "3": "6b604e8368ae0d1f390f6eeb692f63d6a692c46722aa78c72214c59a189f6de3"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m09p06-andrew-exp-s01-c1-4a6b319adb73",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "What if the same bucket feeds several workflows? Send the S three events to EventBridge. The uploader writes the file, and routing rules decide what happens next without changing the uploader.",
          "text_sha256": "4a6b319adb73de2f06af25e24f2e05a8fb3a151c9a78df6a117e4e0c43432545",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "0e553d5fdd79d9a87cc02505f2ef27602511e4823633aea92cda95d8483d3b10",
          "asset_sha256": "8ba94a674d400e16b6810258fa83bae4375e00b24f7cbc47c66ac2475dbe547b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p06-andrew-exp-s01-c2-beea565ac720",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "The rule filters for an S three source and the event type that matters. Match the bucket name and object key as well when only a particular workload should start.",
          "text_sha256": "beea565ac720f436e6905df48c3af48dd7c3f65c308631fa72cbab394eeacbe9",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "00747bbbe41a0abfeb940776078a18b4b4af0ab538fc1ecb79aa77b1043c9ba3",
          "asset_sha256": "8ba94a674d400e16b6810258fa83bae4375e00b24f7cbc47c66ac2475dbe547b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p06-andrew-exp-s01-c3-9c86df0895be",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "This rule checks for my-bucket and the exact key data slash file dot C S V. A different key can arrive on the same bus without starting the workflow, because the filter does not match it.",
          "text_sha256": "9c86df0895be0c00a900675c377eda7f970d081d59100396ceffddf63d40fe97",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "704be56720d9f66302d0a2e580252a636289d211e02af83f020d6d85673a3358",
          "asset_sha256": "8ba94a674d400e16b6810258fa83bae4375e00b24f7cbc47c66ac2475dbe547b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p06-andrew-exp-s01-c4-be4c34832246",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Choose Step Functions for a workflow, SQS for queued work, or Lambda for a function. Permissions and retry behavior still matter, and the consumer should handle repeated delivery safely.",
          "text_sha256": "be4c3483224604e470ffea7389d67da9358c213adc6aa797308f9ed4962685b0",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "be4c3483224604e470ffea7389d67da9358c213adc6aa797308f9ed4962685b0",
          "asset_sha256": "8ba94a674d400e16b6810258fa83bae4375e00b24f7cbc47c66ac2475dbe547b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p06-andrew-exp-s02-c1-a73b8edb0195",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Images, logs, and reports give us different prefixes. S three documents at least thirty-five hundred write-type requests or fifty-five hundred get or head requests per second per partitioned prefix. Distribute parallel load where it fits the access pattern.",
          "text_sha256": "a73b8edb0195a015965f2bd58529c858382630875d3f1abe442b53f0162b4b39",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "d1f698459e30e3cae298673a1959a8c825ff33e64e7b673b065096b338d3f8c2",
          "asset_sha256": "37ca4d9c86dbd60bdf8a4ce35067098edf819dc0743a526f5298df31ede5878c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p06-andrew-exp-s02-c2-0a11038f6b28",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Suppose traffic jumps and S three returns a temporary five-oh-three Slow Down. Back off and retry as the service scales. That response is not evidence the object has disappeared.",
          "text_sha256": "0a11038f6b289aaccf831f20b712a9b24660f8a94b66aa35c083425674f983a4",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "c84fc3ecebcc639f791094e902d59615569b0205dfe4c1e700862f4c59dcf537",
          "asset_sha256": "37ca4d9c86dbd60bdf8a4ce35067098edf819dc0743a526f5298df31ede5878c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p06-andrew-exp-s02-c3-f939b4aa95e4",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "The bucket rate is not the application rate. Check client concurrency, network capacity and, for K M S-backed encryption, applicable K M S request quotas before assuming S three is the bottleneck.",
          "text_sha256": "f939b4aa95e404a50b1a4a46621a539c7ef6658efb4f43bbc31e171d5e3de3fa",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "ddacfea4c16254e0c94f165a6bc99dc4fb08bec83100a512066171ea2bdda95d",
          "asset_sha256": "37ca4d9c86dbd60bdf8a4ce35067098edf819dc0743a526f5298df31ede5878c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p06-andrew-exp-s03-c1-33356126b22a",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "A large upload has more than one request. Start it once to get an upload I D, then use that I D to tie each of the numbered parts to the same transfer.",
          "text_sha256": "33356126b22ab248d148e0ceffb85a530a0c2f6f332abe1863ced618127c56c1",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "5099aac8a3e3f950c8b33c6dd092cca18cd15299ba1c9ba6e98b63ee7e9be452",
          "asset_sha256": "6b604e8368ae0d1f390f6eeb692f63d6a692c46722aa78c72214c59a189f6de3"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p06-andrew-exp-s03-c2-eb015ef258df",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Send numbered parts independently. Keep the returned E tag for each part, because the completion request uses the part numbers and their matching E tags to assemble the object.",
          "text_sha256": "eb015ef258df4c8836990585ced8646481c6ebd9888b8db250d98e0921a248f5",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "6836f87b34daf9676b9f9029793deac1163711d943487ab1ffcbc98aec6a3401",
          "asset_sha256": "6b604e8368ae0d1f390f6eeb692f63d6a692c46722aa78c72214c59a189f6de3"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p06-andrew-exp-s03-c3-9ea06093571a",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Part two failed. What needs to go over the network again? Retry part two under the same upload I D. The successful parts do not have to be resent.",
          "text_sha256": "9ea06093571ad1b281bb95b941bfe67a0bb916d4f02201d7a2d371669a35b9e1",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "7425a4459ed33f17c8ee646895fa6fa97293523d65d04a1f7e8405e2913d9550",
          "asset_sha256": "6b604e8368ae0d1f390f6eeb692f63d6a692c46722aa78c72214c59a189f6de3"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p06-andrew-exp-s03-c4-0eced99a4d08",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Send the ordered part numbers and E tags to complete the upload. Successful part uploads alone do not publish a readable object. The assembled object becomes available once completion succeeds.",
          "text_sha256": "0eced99a4d088bae49395f2bee55a556fe5a721def290dace002c710db22cb91",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "1924c4696c97198cb6a03900e1e17a1739a424acb2b4b0e941dbd51370c044c0",
          "asset_sha256": "6b604e8368ae0d1f390f6eeb692f63d6a692c46722aa78c72214c59a189f6de3"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p06-andrew-exp-s03-c5-b8b5e1e92c0e",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "If this transfer is abandoned instead, abort it to release the stored parts. An unfinished upload is not a complete object.",
          "text_sha256": "b8b5e1e92c0ea3b4a81cd48e8d41becec69504d0c6d84bca2dc51099299d98b9",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "b8b5e1e92c0ea3b4a81cd48e8d41becec69504d0c6d84bca2dc51099299d98b9",
          "asset_sha256": "6b604e8368ae0d1f390f6eeb692f63d6a692c46722aa78c72214c59a189f6de3"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "09",
      "part": "07",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m09p07-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "fd7adcd12cb3cfffbab87e2e7044f1a3cca13d84b66826fef906b5337e6d237b",
        "2": "6daedc0f2812e3744dcc84b3160c40cf6ccc19c8382edc718fbae46e8bc72cc1",
        "3": "01c2a85037c3620457b24ef837d3d711ee60df9030823a0a695b7139b3e6af69"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m09p07-andrew-exp-s01-c1-f88c776567f3",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "The client stopped halfway through this transfer. Its uploaded parts are still stored under an upload I D, so they can cost money even though there is no completed object in the normal listing.",
          "text_sha256": "f88c776567f30b0febf6ef0c8079c564fc2100a2f594e83403b9546458667282",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "2209b0c369a01d179fecf3e5b09cb8444b53e3b2131d42eb17219d97b15f0120",
          "asset_sha256": "fd7adcd12cb3cfffbab87e2e7044f1a3cca13d84b66826fef906b5337e6d237b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p07-andrew-exp-s01-c2-b123d7de3ba3",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Find the upload I D and inspect its parts. If the upload should finish, resume it; if it is abandoned, abort it to remove the stored pieces.",
          "text_sha256": "b123d7de3ba3a601c9a2a23349277a6fd5646f7aec6d54905e7e73dcba6c959b",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "1b5ae794b31454615dc3b5131a7b4ca7553fe5f4dcda0df20d75e1564a818694",
          "asset_sha256": "fd7adcd12cb3cfffbab87e2e7044f1a3cca13d84b66826fef906b5337e6d237b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p07-andrew-exp-s01-c3-d8a6a8eeaa64",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "To clear abandoned transfers automatically, configure Lifecycle to abort incomplete multipart uploads after the chosen age. Expiring a completed object acts on a key, not on these stored upload parts.",
          "text_sha256": "d8a6a8eeaa64dc2f34bcae775cc007ce46a41b702d5bf1fb8d25004de50c0c27",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "d8a6a8eeaa64dc2f34bcae775cc007ce46a41b702d5bf1fb8d25004de50c0c27",
          "asset_sha256": "fd7adcd12cb3cfffbab87e2e7044f1a3cca13d84b66826fef906b5337e6d237b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p07-andrew-exp-s02-c1-afec4ef3a142",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Fetch only the part you need. Requesting the first interval can read a header without downloading the whole object.",
          "text_sha256": "afec4ef3a142edb40463c83c4f55693f405730e9404ea48131d3a547905fd01c",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "afec4ef3a142edb40463c83c4f55693f405730e9404ea48131d3a547905fd01c",
          "asset_sha256": "6daedc0f2812e3744dcc84b3160c40cf6ccc19c8382edc718fbae46e8bc72cc1"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p07-andrew-exp-s02-c2-ed21b6c4406b",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "If the last interval fails, fetch just that interval again. The previous two successful range reads can still be used, provided they belong to the same object version.",
          "text_sha256": "ed21b6c4406b2447fe90ca856d0ce9ac450ff669084ee0fc7d1e7b484309f9f2",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "ed21b6c4406b2447fe90ca856d0ce9ac450ff669084ee0fc7d1e7b484309f9f2",
          "asset_sha256": "6daedc0f2812e3744dcc84b3160c40cf6ccc19c8382edc718fbae46e8bc72cc1"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p07-andrew-exp-s02-c3-321c5df229ba",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "The client reassembles the ranges in order. If the file can change during the download, pin a version or use an appropriate condition. Otherwise, individually successful range reads could return pieces from different object states.",
          "text_sha256": "321c5df229ba69a59d2e59f47bea00b34ad740485216a2fbe7e81ad7be9208bc",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "321c5df229ba69a59d2e59f47bea00b34ad740485216a2fbe7e81ad7be9208bc",
          "asset_sha256": "6daedc0f2812e3744dcc84b3160c40cf6ccc19c8382edc718fbae46e8bc72cc1"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p07-andrew-exp-s03-c1-313923edada0",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "The distant client uploads through the acceleration endpoint. The request enters at an A W S edge location and crosses the A W S network. The object still goes to the bucket in its home Region; this does not make another copy.",
          "text_sha256": "313923edada08494e46576b7a9a7e1485ce72ce1b2631eb33c177799460791d4",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "745e5c536387f79800426c505e1ed630181df02ce9dd76e67cedf6795c939b8a",
          "asset_sha256": "01c2a85037c3620457b24ef837d3d711ee60df9030823a0a695b7139b3e6af69"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p07-andrew-exp-s03-c2-23cfdc65853b",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "You can combine acceleration with multipart upload. The edge endpoint changes the network route; multipart changes how the bytes are split, sent and retried.",
          "text_sha256": "23cfdc65853b3f24f95ae2bf60c9d62ebe4a95f182fedc4f941aa996501e08bc",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "23cfdc65853b3f24f95ae2bf60c9d62ebe4a95f182fedc4f941aa996501e08bc",
          "asset_sha256": "01c2a85037c3620457b24ef837d3d711ee60df9030823a0a695b7139b3e6af69"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p07-andrew-exp-s03-c3-803cab46b431",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Benchmark representative uploads from actual client locations. Compare throughput or latency and weigh the result against acceleration charges.",
          "text_sha256": "803cab46b43112b98c91aca7b434cfbb6d51f480fc607046c92ac651c7c60491",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "803cab46b43112b98c91aca7b434cfbb6d51f480fc607046c92ac651c7c60491",
          "asset_sha256": "01c2a85037c3620457b24ef837d3d711ee60df9030823a0a695b7139b3e6af69"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "09",
      "part": "08",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m09p08-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "ea05934cfdba43016d8da24725d470d4fa442e68813f83c389163f94d7c2827c",
        "2": "9ab00bf01c070080c7da8e5163821be1d714edba2373559406e6e826ca585c80",
        "3": "5201c1e86771eb4ebed654ea9cf8f400e30d326069938f39252cc898c2169eab"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m09p08-andrew-exp-s01-c1-23ff03d7da50",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "A C S V has thousands of rows, but the client needs only a few. In this historical pattern the client sends a S Q L filter to S three Select, which pulls a subset from that one supported object.",
          "text_sha256": "23ff03d7da5069b8e6fcda4f104fa3441adb6b081df9d3e644d325a6f47e083c",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "bd1c7547f0b019c00344d092bef9e55806fc4595c98c285bd3589491697ffc59",
          "asset_sha256": "ea05934cfdba43016d8da24725d470d4fa442e68813f83c389163f94d7c2827c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p08-andrew-exp-s01-c2-b97c3841c50c",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "The client receives matching rows and selected columns. That can cut transfer and processing, but the query still covers one object.",
          "text_sha256": "b97c3841c50c9959be295e00ca357d3df2bdbc618f54fb66843aceb87882752f",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "b97c3841c50c9959be295e00ca357d3df2bdbc618f54fb66843aceb87882752f",
          "asset_sha256": "ea05934cfdba43016d8da24725d470d4fa442e68813f83c389163f94d7c2827c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p08-andrew-exp-s01-c3-4a6af5bb7026",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Check availability before choosing that pattern. S three Select is not available to new customers, though existing customers can continue using it.",
          "text_sha256": "4a6af5bb702667c89e5354eade6c85df68cc5bf99f59b50e0702e4ebd00af8f7",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "4487b882916b3982bdcea4577db20e93bb98e70838535cb1ff770f0514b38e21",
          "asset_sha256": "ea05934cfdba43016d8da24725d470d4fa442e68813f83c389163f94d7c2827c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p08-andrew-exp-s01-c4-51f0a8d1d202",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "For a new data-set query, evaluate Athena or another suitable engine. Check scope and availability before choosing.",
          "text_sha256": "51f0a8d1d20275ad25fa164ef2efaa65a02f58c23d3673b2b15c801afa6f3c06",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "51f0a8d1d20275ad25fa164ef2efaa65a02f58c23d3673b2b15c801afa6f3c06",
          "asset_sha256": "ea05934cfdba43016d8da24725d470d4fa442e68813f83c389163f94d7c2827c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p08-andrew-exp-s02-c1-ac55bb297f03",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Choose a bucket or a prefix or tag filter for Storage Class Analysis. Separate workloads with different access patterns.",
          "text_sha256": "ac55bb297f036c888f299a78445a7e32ff1076e338423bdfd6384f70c9f46bda",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "ac55bb297f036c888f299a78445a7e32ff1076e338423bdfd6384f70c9f46bda",
          "asset_sha256": "9ab00bf01c070080c7da8e5163821be1d714edba2373559406e6e826ca585c80"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p08-andrew-exp-s02-c2-6713aa3a8f9e",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Early data can appear after twenty-four to forty-eight hours, but that does not make it a reliable migration decision. Let the analysis observe access for thirty days or longer before relying on its recommendation.",
          "text_sha256": "6713aa3a8f9ef57bfd2f182a0ac195f0440a2117d586e2decc88e802bc1c03d7",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "6713aa3a8f9ef57bfd2f182a0ac195f0440a2117d586e2decc88e802bc1c03d7",
          "asset_sha256": "9ab00bf01c070080c7da8e5163821be1d714edba2373559406e6e826ca585c80"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p08-andrew-exp-s02-c3-75171bd93b54",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "If the observed access suggests that Standard Infrequent Access would be cheaper, decide whether the retrieval and billing tradeoffs fit. Then configure a separate Lifecycle rule. Running the analysis never moves the objects by itself.",
          "text_sha256": "75171bd93b5435750aff37393ba64bf6d4b4c253c880cc37b4eeaac43edab561",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "75171bd93b5435750aff37393ba64bf6d4b4c253c880cc37b4eeaac43edab561",
          "asset_sha256": "9ab00bf01c070080c7da8e5163821be1d714edba2373559406e6e826ca585c80"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p08-andrew-exp-s03-c1-5cdb05bfa5be",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Storage Lens aggregates storage signals across the scopes shown, from organization and accounts down to buckets and, when enabled, prefixes. Use the level that helps you identify where the problem is concentrated.",
          "text_sha256": "5cdb05bfa5bef10e84085d71c69c15813f29c5c75f7fa05225545810b99431dc",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "5cdb05bfa5bef10e84085d71c69c15813f29c5c75f7fa05225545810b99431dc",
          "asset_sha256": "5201c1e86771eb4ebed654ea9cf8f400e30d326069938f39252cc898c2169eab"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p08-andrew-exp-s03-c2-23155553ca02",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "The dashboard can point to a bucket with unusual growth. Use that signal to decide where to investigate, not as an automatic instruction to change retention or delete files.",
          "text_sha256": "23155553ca02c7f9acc69aa5e22e1632970c22bf0cdbf9c45e4d753e856d8824",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "23155553ca02c7f9acc69aa5e22e1632970c22bf0cdbf9c45e4d753e856d8824",
          "asset_sha256": "5201c1e86771eb4ebed654ea9cf8f400e30d326069938f39252cc898c2169eab"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p08-andrew-exp-s03-c3-f2fa24d5dc4b",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "The default account dashboard is preconfigured. Create a custom dashboard when you need a narrower scope, such as selected Regions or buckets, instead of assuming one view fits every investigation.",
          "text_sha256": "f2fa24d5dc4b2a9f2f8623d281a80f698ddd82e4f7da613a7a1bb240245e15ae",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "f2fa24d5dc4b2a9f2f8623d281a80f698ddd82e4f7da613a7a1bb240245e15ae",
          "asset_sha256": "5201c1e86771eb4ebed654ea9cf8f400e30d326069938f39252cc898c2169eab"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p08-andrew-exp-s03-c4-5c0a7913ffa9",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "The dashboard is not the only evidence source. A daily C S V or Parquet export to an authorized S three destination allows further analysis over time.",
          "text_sha256": "5c0a7913ffa926dd516899b6515ad516888fb6ab29c49ce007d452f02211b9db",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "7c3e75d0be3b59b038573b7eb0320361cb2c992c23b00324c88af5bc48028149",
          "asset_sha256": "5201c1e86771eb4ebed654ea9cf8f400e30d326069938f39252cc898c2169eab"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
